Syntax: cast 'faerie fog'

Faerie Fog summons a thick cloud of enchanted purple vapor that fills the
immediate area around the caster. This mystical fog has the unique property
of seeking out and clinging to invisible creatures, outlining their forms
and revealing them to normal sight.

The spell creates a billowing cloud that spreads throughout the room,
penetrating magical concealment that would foil ordinary detection methods.
Creatures hidden by invisibility spells, potions, or natural abilities are
exposed when the fog touches them.

Unlike dispel invisible, faerie fog does not permanently remove the
invisibility enchantment - it merely makes the invisible visible for a
time by coating them in luminescent particles. Once the fog dissipates,
creatures may regain their concealment if the underlying magic persists.

The fog is centered on the caster and affects all invisible creatures in
the room regardless of allegiance, potentially revealing hidden allies as
well as enemies.

See Also: DETECT INVISIBLE, DISPEL INVISIBLE, TRUE SIGHT
